!! Command listener

We used the ''environment'' setting to guide us in our refactoring journey. We can now go on with the next settings to migrate, the ones needed by the command listener:

- Error behavior
- STOMP host
- STOMP port
- STOMP user name
- STOMP user password
- Queue name
- Durable subscription
- ACK policy
- Prefetch count
- Timeout
- STOMP client in debug mode
- Restart on error

We'll start by using an adapter for each one of them, similarly as what we've done with the ''environment'' setting.
Later, we might want to introduce a way to group ports together. The ==EDAApplication== settings won't be affected, but the ==EDAPortSettingsPort== will become quickly unmanageable otherwise.

!!! Error behavior

This setting, due to its nature, does not allow any adapter but a predefined list.
Anyway, for the sake of consistency, let's avoid dealing with particular cases.
After adding this adapter class setting to ''portSettingsOn:under:on:'' in ==EDASettings== we get:

% ${changes:path=code/001-EDASettings_class_portSettingsOn_under_on_.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
portSettingsOn: aBuilder under: aParent on: app
	| entry environmentValues key portResolver commandListenerErrorStrategyValues |
	key := aParent , 'ports'.
	entry := aBuilder group: key.
	entry
		label: 'Ports' translated;
		parent: aParent.
	portResolver := EDAPortResolver new.
	environmentValues := OrderedCollection
		withAll:
			(portResolver availableEnvironmentSettingsAdapters
				collect:
					[ :adapterClass | adapterClass description translated -> adapterClass ]).
	(aBuilder pickOne: #environmentSettingsAdapterClass)
		label: 'Environment adapter' translated;
		target: app portSettingsPort;
		parent: key;
		domainValues: environmentValues.
	commandListenerErrorStrategyValues := OrderedCollection
		withAll:
			(portResolver availableCommandListenerErrorStrategyAdapters
				collect:
					[ :adapterClass | adapterClass description translated -> adapterClass ]).
	(aBuilder pickOne: #commandListenerErrorStrategyAdapterClass)
		label: 'Error strategy' translated;
		target: app portSettingsPort;
		parent: key;
		domainValues: commandListenerErrorStrategyValues
]]]

This method is becoming too large, but we'll refactor it soon enough. Using Pharo's debugger-driven development, we'll be asked to create the missing method ''availableCommandListenerErrorStrategyAdapters'' in ==EDAPortResolver==. Let's create it, but in ==EDATPortResolver== trait instead.

% ${changes:path=code/002-EDASTPortResolver_availableCommandListenerErrorStrategyAdapters.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
availableCommandListenerErrorStrategyAdapters
	^ self
		availableAdapters: EDASCommandListenerErrorStrategySettingsPort
]]]

We need to create the new trait as well.

% ${changes:path=code/003-EDASCommandListenerErrorStrategySettingsPort.ombu}
[[[classDefinition=true
Trait named: #EDATCommandListenerErrorStrategySettingsPort
	 uses: EDASSettingsPort
	 package: 'EDA-Settings-Ports'
]]]

Opening ==SettingBrowser== again will detect a missing method. We told ==SettingBrowser== ==EDAPortSettingsPort== can deal with ''commandListenerErrorStrategyAdapterClass'', but it doesn't. Let's add the new attribute and accessors to the class.

% ${changes:path=code/004-EDASPortSettingsPort.ombu}
[[[classDefinition=true
Object subclass: #EDASPortSettingsPort
	instanceVariableNames: 'announcer environmentSettingsPort environmentSettingsAdapterClass commandListenerErrorStrategyAdapterClass'
	classVariableNames: ''
	package: 'EDA-Settings-Ports'
]]]

% ${changes:path=code/005-EDASPortSettingsPort_commandListenerErrorStrategyAdapterClass.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
commandListenerErrorStrategyAdapterClass
	^ commandListenerErrorStrategyAdapterClass
]]]

% ${changes:path=code/006-EDASPortSettingsPort_commandListenerErrorStrategyAdapterClass_.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
commandListenerErrorStrategyAdapterClass: anObject
	commandListenerErrorStrategyAdapterClass := anObject
]]]

Since we don't expect more than one adapter class, we won't emit a new event when the port changes.
We need to implement the only adapter: a predefined list of strategies.

% ${changes:path=code/007-EDASPredefinedCommandListenerErrorStrategyInMemoryAdapter.ombu}
[[[classDefinition=true
Object subclass: #EDASPredefinedCommandListenerErrorStrategyInMemoryAdapter
	uses: EDASCommandListenerErrorStrategySettingsPort
	instanceVariableNames: 'strategyName edaApplication'
	classVariableNames: ''
	package: 'EDA-Settings-Adapters-InMemory'
]]]

The setting value is stored in the ''errorStrategy'' attribute.

% ${changes:path=code/008-EDASPredefinedCommandListenerErrorStrategyInMemoryAdapter_strategyName.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
strategyName
	^ errorStrategy
		ifNil: [ self strategyName: self availableStrategies first.
			strategy ]
]]]

% ${changes:path=code/009-EDASPredefinedCommandListenerErrorStrategyInMemoryAdapter_strategyName_.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
strategyName: anObject
	strategyName := anObject
]]]

The ''availableStrategies'' can be implemented on the class side.

% ${changes:path=code/010-EDASPredefinedCommandListenerErrorStrategyInMemoryAdapter_availableStrategies.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
availableStrategies
	^ self class availableStrategies
]]]

% ${changes:path=code/011-EDASPredefinedCommandListenerErrorStrategyInMemoryAdapter_class_availableStrategies.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
availableStrategies
	^ EDAEErrorHandlingStrategy subclasses collect: [ :s | s name ]
]]]

We need the new adapter to provide a description.

% ${changes:path=code/012-EDASPredefinedCommandListenerErrorStrategyInMemoryAdapter_class_description.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
description
	^ 'Predefined list of error handling strategies for incoming commands'
]]]

Finally, we can enable it.

% ${changes:path=code/013-EDASPredefinedCommandListenerErrorStrategyInMemoryAdapter_class_accepts_.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
accepts: aPort
	^ aPort = EDASCommandListenerErrorStrategySettingsPort
]]]

Let's now add this setting back to our tree.

% ${changes:path=code/014-EDASSettings_class_edaSettingsOn_for_under_.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
edaSettingsOn: aBuilder for: anEDAApplication under: aSymbol
	| parent parentGroup |
	parent := anEDAApplication applicationName.
	parentGroup := aBuilder group: parent.
	parentGroup
		label: parent translated;
		parent: aSymbol;
		description: parent;
		noOrdering.
	self
		environmentSettingsOn: aBuilder
		under: parent
		on: anEDAApplication.
	self
		commandListenerErrorStrategySettingsOn: aBuilder
		under: parent
		on: anEDAApplication.
]]]

==EDAApplication== needs to include a reference to its own port storing the settings related to the command listener error strategy.

% ${changes:path=code/015-EDAApplication.ombu}
[[[classDefinition=true
Object subclass: #EDAApplication
	uses: EDATLogging
	instanceVariableNames: 'commandConsumer commandDispatcher eventAnnouncer eventProducer eventStore isConfigured isStarted projectorsByTenant applicationName portSettingsPort environmentSettingsPort commandListenerErrorStrategySettingsPort settingsAnnouncer'
	classVariableNames: 'ProjectionSynchronizationEnabled'
	package: 'EDA-Application'
]]]

The getter accessor uses lazy-loading.
% ${changes:path=code/016-EDAApplication_commandListenerErrorStrategySettingsPort.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
EDAApplication >> commandListenerErrorStrategySettingsPort
	^ self portSettingsPort commandListenerErrorStrategySettingsPort
]]]

The setter accessor is just the default.

% ${changes:path=code/016-EDAApplication_commandListenerErrorStrategySettingsPort_.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
commandListenerErrorStrategySettingsPort: anAdapter
	anAdapter = self portSettingsPort commandListenerErrorStrategySettingsPort
              ifTrue: [ ^ self ]
              ifFalse: [ self portSettingsPort commandListenerErrorStrategySettingsPort: anAdapter ]
]]]

If we check the value associated to the ==EDAApplication== after we change the strategy in the settings, we can see it gets the actual class.

[[[methodDefinition=false
EDAApplications uniqueInstance edaApplications first commandListenerErrorStrategySettingsPort strategy
]]]

!!! Stomp Topic Listener

We'll add two new classes, meant to store the actual settings used by ==EDAApplication==.

% ${changes:path=code/017-EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter.ombu}
[[[classDefinition=true
Object subclass: #EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter
	uses: EDASInMemoryAdapter
	instanceVariableNames: 'host port username password timeout debug durable restartOnError edaApplication'
	classVariableNames: ''
	package: 'EDA-Settings-Adapters-InMemory'
]]]

==EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter== will contain the shared properties of both listener and publisher.

Let's generate the accessors as usual.

% ${changes:path=code/018-EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter_host.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter >> host
    ^ host
]]]

% ${changes:path=code/019-EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter_host_.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter >> host: anObject
    host := anObject
]]]

% ${changes:path=code/020-EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter_port.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter >> port
    ^ port
]]]

% ${changes:path=code/021-EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter_port_.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter >> port: anInteger
    port := anInteger
]]]

% ${changes:path=code/022-EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter_username.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter >> username
    ^ username
]]]

% ${changes:path=code/023-EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter_username_.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter >> username: aString
    username := aString
]]]

% ${changes:path=code/024-EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter_password.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter >> password
    ^ password
]]]

% ${changes:path=code/025-EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter_password_.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter >> password: aString
    password := aString
]]]


% ${changes:path=code/026-EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter_timeout.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter >> timeout
    ^ timeout
]]]

% ${changes:path=code/027-EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter_timeout_.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter >> timeout: anInteger
    timeout := anInteger
]]]

% ${changes:path=code/030-EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter_debug.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter >> debug
    ^ debug
]]]

% ${changes:path=code/031-EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter_debug_.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter >> debug: aBoolean
    debug := aBoolean
]]]

% ${changes:path=code/032-EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter_durable.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter >> durable
    ^ durable
]]]

% ${changes:path=code/033-EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter_durable_.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter >> durable: aBoolean
    durable := aBoolean
]]]

% ${changes:path=code/034-EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter_restartOnError.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter >> restartOnError
    ^ restartOnError
]]]

% ${changes:path=code/035-EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter_restartOnError_.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter >> restartOnError: aBoolean
    restartOnError := aBoolean
]]]

% ${changes:path=code/036-EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter_edaApplication.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter >> edaApplication
    ^ edaApplication
]]]

% ${changes:path=code/037-EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter_edaApplication_.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter >> edaApplication: anObject
    edaApplication := anObject
]]]

Now we can focus on the Stomp listener adapter.

% ${changes:path=code/038-EDASStompTopicListenerSettingsInMemoryAdapter.ombu}
[[[classDefinition=true
EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter subclass: #EDASStompTopicListenerSettingsInMemoryAdapter
	uses: EDASCommandListenerSettingsPort
	instanceVariableNames: 'topicListener prefetchCount ack queue errorStrategy'
	classVariableNames: ''
	package: 'EDAS-Settings-Adapters-InMemory'
]]]

Again, the accessors are straight forward.

% ${changes:path=code/39-EDASStompTopicListenerSettingsInMemoryAdapter_topicListener.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
EDASStompTopicListenerSettingsInMemoryAdapter >> topicListener
    ^ topicListener
]]]

% ${changes:path=code/40-EDASStompTopicListenerSettingsInMemoryAdapter_topicListener_.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
EDASStompTopicListenerSettingsInMemoryAdapter >> topicListener: anObject
    topicListener := anObject
]]]

% ${changes:path=code/41-EDASStompTopicListenerSettingsInMemoryAdapter_prefetchCount.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
EDASStompTopicListenerSettingsInMemoryAdapter >> prefetchCount
    ^ prefetchCount
]]]

% ${changes:path=code/42-EDASStompTopicListenerSettingsInMemoryAdapter_prefetchCount_.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
EDASStompTopicListenerSettingsInMemoryAdapter >> prefetchCount: anInteger
    prefetchCount := anInteger
]]]

% ${changes:path=code/43-EDASStompTopicListenerSettingsInMemoryAdapter_ack.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
EDASStompTopicListenerSettingsInMemoryAdapter >> ack
    ^ ack
]]]

% ${changes:path=code/44-EDASStompTopicListenerSettingsInMemoryAdapter_ack_.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
EDASStompTopicListenerSettingsInMemoryAdapter >> ack: aSymbol
    ack := aSymbol
]]]

% ${changes:path=code/45-EDASStompTopicListenerSettingsInMemoryAdapter_queue.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
EDASStompTopicListenerSettingsInMemoryAdapter >> queue
    ^ queue
]]]

% ${changes:path=code/46-EDASStompTopicListenerSettingsInMemoryAdapter_queue_.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
EDASStompTopicListenerSettingsInMemoryAdapter >> queue: aString
    queue := aString
]]]

% ${changes:path=code/47-EDASStompTopicListenerSettingsInMemoryAdapter_errorStrategy.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
EDASStompTopicListenerSettingsInMemoryAdapter >> errorStrategy
    ^ errorStrategy
]]]

% ${changes:path=code/48-EDASStompTopicListenerSettingsInMemoryAdapter_errorStrategy_.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
EDASStompTopicListenerSettingsInMemoryAdapter >> errorStrategy: anObject
    errorStrategy := anObject
]]]

You might have noticed the method ''restartOnError'' gets injected both by the ==EDASCommandListenerSettingsPort== trait and the ==EDASStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter== parent class.
In cases like this, the trait's behavior prevails. We need to call parent's behavior explicitly.

% ${changes:path=code/49-EDASStompTopicListenerSettingsInMemoryAdapter_restartOnError.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
EDASStompTopicListenerSettingsInMemoryAdapter >> restartOnError
    ^ super restartOnError
]]]


==EDASettings== can now export the command listener group.

% ${changes:path=code/036-EDASettings_class_commandListenerSettingsOn_under_on_.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
commandListenerSettingsOn: aBuilder under: parent on: app
	| key |
	key := parent , 'commandListener'.
	(aBuilder group: key)
		label: 'Command Listener' translated;
		description: 'Command listener';
		parent: parent.
	^ self
		settingOn: aBuilder
		named: #commandListenerErrorStrategy
		labelled: 'Command Consuming Error'
		withDescription: 'Strategy when dealing with command consuming errors'
		usingConfig: app commandListenerSettingsPort
		under: key
		on: app
]]]

We need to implement the ports for both the group and the specific setting.

% ${changes:path=code/022-EDATCommandListenerErrorStrategySettingsPort.ombu}
[[[classDefinition=true
Trait named: #EDATCommandListenerErrorStrategySettingsPort
	 uses: EDATSettingsPort
	 package: 'EDA-Settings-Ports'
]]]


% ${changes:path=code/028-EDAStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter_prefetchCount.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
EDAStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter >> prefetchCount
    ^ prefetchCount
]]]

% ${changes:path=code/029-EDAStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter_prefetchCount_.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
EDAStompSettingsInMemoryAdapter >> prefetchCount: anInteger
    prefetchCount := anInteger
]]]
